:'''Caenis:''' Welcome back to the hub of the Demigod Council, Lord Anaxagoras.
:'''Caenis:''' Surely you remember that countless eloquent orators have stood in this spot before and emerged victorious by stoking public sentiment with their words. And yet, there have also been innumerable blasphemous philosophers who set themselves up for failure because they refused to defend their actions.
:'''Caenis:''' This tiny stage is the most profound embodiment of Okhema in centuries. In fifteen days, this site shall also become the most important, as well as the final turning point in Okhema's history...
:'''Caenis:''' {{Цвет|Ключевой|nobold=1|May the both of us carry out our duties with honor and lead the masses back toward the Era Chrysea, a golden age with no Death, Strife, or Trickery.}}
:'''Cerces:''' Oh my, fifteen days and nights... that aligns perfectly with the date of your demise. Could such a coincidence truly exist?
:'''Anaxa:''' Using death to prove myself fits my intentions perfectly.
:'''Caenis:''' What strong conviction you have! As expected of the hero who dared to stand up to the Goldweaver.
:'''Cerces:''' Hehe... As expected, she misunderstands you.
:'''Anaxa:''' That's enough, Lady Caenis. Dispense with the niceties. I only accepted your invitation so that I can serve the commoners alongside the members of the Council of Elders. Don't test my patience with such superfluous formalities.
:'''Caenis:''' You say that now, but surely you also require my aid as well, so that you can stay alive, even when being pursued by the golden thread?
:'''Anaxa:''' You worry too much. She won't show her hand too freely, as she still needs to garner support from the masses at the citizens' assembly.
:'''Caenis:''' Even someone like me can tell that only a sliver of her humanity remains. Surely you're not asserting that she will definitely act in a rational manner?
:'''Anaxa:''' As you're no doubt aware, Aglaea covets the Coreflame that I possess, which makes it the bargaining chip that allows me and the rest of you to negotiate with her. However, in return, I'll need the Council of Elders to support me as much as possible. Naturally, this includes the guards as well.
:'''Anaxa:''' You're well aware how valuable {{Rubi|Cerces|Reason Titan}}' Coreflame will be in the Era Chrysea that you are desperately pursuing...
:'''Anaxa:''' Talk is cheap, so you'd better act prudently as well.
:'''Caenis:''' I understand. After all, this battle of wits is just a means for each party to acquire what they need. As long as your request is reasonable, the Council of Elders never shortchanges its allies. Since we're both intent on mutual cooperation, let's not mince words and just speak plainly to each other...
:'''Caenis:''' Let us decide how much we can secure for ourselves and how much we're willing to sacrifice, like true philosophers &mdash; with our words and wisdom.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Let's begin, then.
